<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the Friday to Sunday period, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final numbers will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Space Jam ................... $29.3 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Ransom ...................... $23.0 million</p>
<p>    3 (*) The Mirror Has Two Faces .... $12.2 million</p>
<p>    4 (4) Set It Off ..................  $5.8 million</p>
<p>    5 (2) Romeo &amp; Juliet ..............  $5.6 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) Sleepers ....................  $2.3 million</p>
<p>    7 (5) High School High ............. $1.6 million</p>
<p>    8 (6) The First Wives Club ......... $1.58 million</p>
<p>    9 (8) The Ghost and the Darkness ... $1.0 million</p>
<p>   10(10) Michael Collins .............. $850,000</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Space Jam,&quot; &quot;Sleepers&quot; and &quot;Michael Collins&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.. &quot;Ransom&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;The Mirror Has Two Faces&quot; and &quot;High School High&quot; are released by Sony Corp.. &quot;Set It Off&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner. &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; is released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;The First Wives Club&quot; and &quot;The Ghost and the Darkness&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
